    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="09598121-299e-545c-8b33-01f5243f3023" activityNameId="685994be-00ba-590a-ac67-2eeda195a696" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Uranium conversion plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Uranium conversion plant
Data for material and energy requirements for construction and decommissioning are from an old study, which does not differenciate between dry and wet process. The material inventory may not correspond to currently operating facilities, which is taken into account in the uncertainties. The land use is based on actual data for the Sequoyah facility. The lifetime is assumed to be 40 years with a throughput of 5000 t/a. Although Sequoyah was operating only for 22 years, 40 years can be assumed as an average for currently operating plants.;
UUID: 3e12912d-79d7-335a-999d-791a5313ac69
The module includes: land use of the factory; energy (electricity and diesel) and material requirements for the construction of the facility; transport requirements during construction; energy and transport requirements (for non-contaminated inerts concrete with reinforcing bars) during decommissioning; disposal of the non-contaminated inerts. The non contaminated metals are assumed to be recycled
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Available construction material and energy data refer to conditions in early 1980s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3e12912d-79d7-335a-999d-791a5313ac69.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
